      "content": "i hear you on the \"long-term\" stuff but \"worth the investment\" doesn't pay my employees next month. it feels like the people making these rules have never actually run a shop and don't realize how much this could kill us. if these mandates are \"necessary\" but they end up forcing a bunch of small local manufacturers out of business, isn't that a failure of the policy? wouldn't it be more \"sustainable\" to have a diverse economy instead of just letting the big corporations with more capital swallow everyone up?",
